@page "/portal/sessions"
@namespace Burbuja.Portal.Components.Pages
@inject PortalData Data
@inject TimeProvider Clock
@inject IEnumerable<IPortalSessionLabel> Labels

@*
    M14 R6 — Sessions is ONE list.

    **What was wrong.** The page answered "what is running" three times: a pomnibot grid, an Agents grid, an
    Agents `jobs` grid, and under them a "Rails" card grouping the same resources by workspace. Four
    presentations of one question, and the reader had to know which KIND they were looking for before they
    could look — which is the opposite of what an index is for. A person arriving at `/portal/sessions` wants
    one list of what exists, with the kind on each row, and then to filter by it.

    **What one list costs, and how it is paid.** The three kinds do not share a shape: a job has a workspace and
    a start time, an agent has a driver and no workspace, a pomnibot job has a repo and costs in a different
    ledger. So the list has one column per fact a reader compares (`tipo · nombre · dónde · estado · modelo ·
    coste · desde`) and a kind renders `—` for what it does not have — the same rule every other page keeps, and
    the alternative (three grids) is what this round removed. Nothing is summed across kinds: the pomnibot
    ledger is not the Agents ledger, and a total that added them would be a number no host booked.

    **The Rails card is gone.** It grouped the same rows by workspace / repo, which the shell's rail and
    `/portal/workspaces` already do; a second grouping of one list is how a page becomes four screens again.

    **What the page says when a kind is absent.** `_sources` names what was read and what was NOT, because an
    empty host and a host whose `Burbuja.Pomnibot` is not registered look identical in a list that simply has
    fewer rows.

    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    M15 item 13 — the list is grouped by workspace, and it still has ONE `<table>` because two facts outside
    this lane pin exactly one `table.grid` on the page (`PomnibotTests` and `SessionsPageTests`).

    **Grouping without a second table, and without inventing a row.** A group heading drawn as its own `<tr>`
    would be a row the grid does not have, and `SessionsPageTests` counts `tbody tr`; so the grouping is carried
    by the WORKSPACE column: every row still names its workspace, and the FIRST row of each group carries the
    group's label (`grid-group-label`). Rows are ordered by group, so a workspace's rows are adjacent.

    **Product annotations state their provenance.** A registered label contributor may interpret a product's
    naming convention; the generic list never infers a stored relationship from a runtime name.

    **The warning dot is the record's own pending state.** The host serves `pendingApprovalId` on agents, jobs
    and pomnibot jobs (and an agent's `inbox`); the dot is drawn from exactly those fields, never from a status
    this page inferred. The explicit `awaitingApproval` word the kernel writes is honoured as a fallback, and
    nothing else is.
*@

<PageTitle>Sessions</PageTitle>

<PageHeader Eyebrow="Monitor" Title="Sessions" Loaded="@(!_loading)"
            Subtitle="Everything this host is running — jobs, agents and pomnibot jobs — in one list grouped by workspace, with the kind on every row." />

<ErrorAlert Failure="_failure" />

@if (_failure is null)
{
    <Card Title="Everything that runs" Subtitle="@_sources">
        @if (_loading)
        {
            <LoadingState Text="reading jobs, agents and pomnibot jobs…" />
        }
        else if (_rows.Count == 0)
        {
            <EmptyState Text="No job, agent, or pomnibot job in this resource group. This list shows what the host already has; there is nothing else to read." />
        }
        else
        {
            <div class="row row-wrap" style="margin-bottom: 8px">
                <input class="input sessions-filter" aria-label="filter sessions" placeholder="filter by name, workspace or context" @bind="Filter" @bind:event="oninput" />
            </div>
            @if (Filtered.Count == 0)
            {
                <EmptyState Text="Nothing in this list matches the filter. Clear it to see every row the host served." />
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="grid-scroll"><QuickGrid Items="Filtered.AsQueryable()" Class="grid">
                    <PropertyColumn Property="r => r.Kind" Title="kind" Sortable="true" />
                    <PropertyColumn Property="r => r.Name" Title="name" Sortable="true" />
                    @* The workspace column IS the grouping: the first row of each group carries the label. *@
                    <TemplateColumn Title="workspace">
                        <ChildContent Context="row">
                            @if (row.GroupFirst)
                            {
                                <span class="grid-group-label" title="rows are ordered and grouped by workspace; this is the group's first row">@row.Group</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span class="muted">@row.Where</span>
                            }
                        </ChildContent>
                    </TemplateColumn>
                    <TemplateColumn Title="state" Sortable="true" SortBy="@(GridSort<Row>.ByAscending(r => r.State))">
                        <ChildContent Context="row">
                            @if (row.PendingWhy is { Length: > 0 } why)
                            {
                                <span class="warn-dot" role="img" aria-label="@why" title="@why">●</span>
                            }
                            <span class="pill @StatusPill.Tone(row.State)">@row.State</span>
                        </ChildContent>
                    </TemplateColumn>
                    <TemplateColumn Title="turn">
                        <ChildContent Context="row">
                            @if (row.TurnLabel is { Length: > 0 } label)
                            {
                                <span class="turn-label" title="Product-provided provenance; the label states its source.">@label</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span class="muted small">—</span>
                            }
                        </ChildContent>
                    </TemplateColumn>
                    <PropertyColumn Property="r => r.Model" Title="model" />
                    <PropertyColumn Property="r => r.Cost" Title="cost" />
                    <PropertyColumn Property="r => r.Since" Title="since" Sortable="true" />
                    <TemplateColumn Title="" Align="Align.Right">
                        <ChildContent Context="row">
                            <a class="btn btn-small" href="@row.Href">open</a>
                        </ChildContent>
                    </TemplateColumn>
                </QuickGrid></div>
            }
        }
    </Card>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// One row of the list. <see cref="Kind"/> is what makes one list possible: the reader filters by reading
    /// it, and a column a kind does not have renders an em dash rather than a blank that reads as a bug.
    ///
    /// <para><see cref="Group"/> is the scope the row is grouped under (a job's workspace, an agent's bound
    /// workspace or <c>(unbound)</c>, a pomnibot job's repo), and <see cref="GroupFirst"/> is set on the first
    /// row of each group by <see cref="Filtered"/> — a positional member so the view can be built with
    /// <c>with</c> and the loaded list is never mutated.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private sealed record Row(
        string Kind,
        string Name,
        string Where,
        string State,
        string Model,
        string Cost,
        string Since,
        string Href,
        string Group,
        string? TurnLabel,
        string? PendingWhy,
        bool GroupFirst = false);

    private PortalFailure? _failure;

    /// <summary>
    /// True until the projections have been read. It exists because the page used to render its three
    /// "Nothing here." empty states while the reads were still in flight, and an empty state that means
    /// "not loaded yet" is indistinguishable from one that means "there is nothing" — measured in the Pi
    /// compose lane, where G7 screenshotted exactly that page (`No jobs in this resource group.` with a
    /// succeeded job in the store) and then failed to find the row it had just created. The grid is
    /// empty of "open" links until the data lands; a loading line is the honest thing to draw.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _loading = true;

    private List<Row> _rows = [];

    /// <summary>What was read, and what was not — an empty kind and an absent provider are different hosts.</summary>
    private string _sources = "reading…";

    /// <summary>The filter box's text. Empty means "every row".</summary>
    private string _filter = "";

    private string Filter
    {
        get => _filter;
        set => _filter = value;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The rows the grid renders: filtered, then re-labelled so the first row of each group is the only one
    /// carrying the group heading — including after a filter, where a group can lose rows and still needs its
    /// label. A match is a name, a workspace/repo or a persona/turn label; the row's KIND is deliberately not
    /// searched, because the kind is what the reader is looking AT, not what they are looking FOR.
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<Row> Filtered
    {
        get
        {
            var needle = _filter.Trim();
            IEnumerable<Row> rows = _rows;
            if (needle.Length > 0)
            {
                rows = rows.Where(r =>
                    r.Name.Contains(needle, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                    || r.Where.Contains(needle, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                    || r.Group.Contains(needle, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                    || (r.TurnLabel?.Contains(needle, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ?? false));
            }

            var grouped = new List<Row>();
            string? previous = null;
            foreach (var row in rows)
            {
                grouped.Add(row with { GroupFirst = !string.Equals(previous, row.Group, StringComparison.Ordinal) });
                previous = row.Group;
            }

            return grouped;
        }
    }

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var ct = CancellationToken.None;
        try
        {
            var (scope, failure) = await Data.ResolveScopeAsync(ct);
            _failure = failure;
            if (scope is null)
                return;

            var workspaces = (await Data.WorkspacesAsync(scope, ct))
                .Where(w => w.Id is { Length: > 0 } && w.Name is { Length: > 0 })
                .Select(w => (Id: w.Id!, Name: w.Name!))
                .ToList();

            foreach (var job in await Data.JobsAsync(scope, ct))
            {
                var id = job.Id ?? "";
                var workspaceName = workspaces
                    .FirstOrDefault(w => id.StartsWith(w.Id + "/jobs/", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                    .Name ?? "?";
                var pending = PendingWhy(
                    job.Properties?.PendingApprovalId,
                    inbox: false,
                    awaitingStatus: string.Equals(job.Properties?.Status, "awaitingApproval", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));
                _rows.Add(new Row(
                    "job",
                    job.Name ?? "?",
                    workspaceName,
                    job.Properties?.Status ?? "unknown",
                    job.Properties?.AgentId ?? "—",
                    PortalData.Money(job.Properties?.Cost.TotalUsd),
                    job.Properties?.StartedAt?.UtcDateTime.ToString("MM-dd HH:mm:ss'Z'", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) ?? "—",
                    $"/portal/jobs/{Uri.EscapeDataString(workspaceName)}/{Uri.EscapeDataString(job.Name ?? "")}",
                    workspaceName,
                    null,
                    pending));
            }

            foreach (var agent in await Data.AgentsAsync(scope, ct))
            {
                // The agent's bound workspace when the record holds one — the same pair the rail groups by —
                // and `(unbound)` when it does not, which is a truthful group rather than a dropped row.
                var workspace = agent.Properties?.WorkspaceId is { Length: > 0 } bound
                    ? bound
                    : agent.Properties?.ComputeWorkspaceId is { Length: > 0 } compute ? compute : "";
                var pending = PendingWhy(
                    agent.Properties?.PendingApprovalId,
                    inbox: agent.Properties?.Inbox is { Count: > 0 },
                    awaitingStatus: false);
                _rows.Add(new Row(
                    "agent",
                    agent.Name ?? "?",
                    workspace.Length > 0 ? workspace : "—",
                    agent.Properties?.State ?? "unknown",
                    agent.Properties?.ModelId ?? agent.Properties?.Driver ?? "—",
                    PortalData.Money(agent.Properties?.CostUsd),
                    "—",
                    $"/portal/agents/{Uri.EscapeDataString(agent.Name ?? "")}",
                    workspace.Length > 0 ? workspace : "(unbound)",
                    SessionLabel(agent.Name),
                    pending));
            }

            var pomnibot = await LoadPomnibotAsync(scope, ct);

            // Grouped order: a stable sort so a workspace's rows are adjacent without re-ordering the kinds
            // within a group on every render.
            _rows = [.. _rows
                .OrderBy(r => r.Group, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                .ThenBy(r => r.Kind, StringComparer.Ordinal)
                .ThenBy(r => r.Name, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)];

            _sources = pomnibot.Absent
                ? "read jobs and agents; Burbuja.Pomnibot is not registered on this host, so no pomnibot jobs are in the list"
                : $"read jobs, agents and pomnibot jobs — {Text.Plural(_rows.Count, "row", "rows")}, each with its kind, grouped by workspace";
        }
        catch (ArmException ex)
        {
            _failure = PortalFailure.From(ex);
        }
        finally
        {
            _loading = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// A host with no <c>Burbuja.Pomnibot</c> namespace is normal (the Agents-only build), so the list says so
    /// rather than failing the page — the same tolerance the dashboard has.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task<(bool Absent, int Count)> LoadPomnibotAsync(ArmScope scope, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        IReadOnlyList<PortalEnvelope<PortalPomnibotJob>> jobs;
        try
        {
            jobs = await Data.PomnibotJobsAsync(scope, ct);
        }
        catch (ArmException ex) when (PortalData.IsTypeAbsent(ex))
        {
            return (true, 0);
        }

        var now = Clock.GetUtcNow();
        foreach (var job in jobs)
        {
            var repo = job.Properties?.Spec.RepoId is { Length: > 0 } bound ? bound : "(no repo)";
            var status = job.Properties?.ExecutionStatus;
            var pending = PendingWhy(
                job.Properties?.PendingApprovalId,
                inbox: false,
                awaitingStatus: PortalData.IsPomnibotAwaitingApproval(status));
            _rows.Add(new Row(
                "pomnibot",
                job.Name ?? "?",
                repo,
                // The pomnibot RP's own word: `executionStatus` when it has one, the envelope's
                // provisioning state otherwise. Never a status this page invented.
                status ?? job.ProvisioningState ?? "unknown",
                job.Properties?.Spec.Model ?? "—",
                PortalData.Money(job.Properties?.Cost.TotalUsd),
                PortalData.Age(PortalData.CreatedAt(job), now),
                $"/portal/pomnibot/jobs/{Uri.EscapeDataString(job.Name ?? "")}",
                $"pomnibot, {repo}",
                SessionLabel(job.Name),
                pending));
        }

        return (false, jobs.Count);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Why a row carries the warning dot, or null when it does not. Every branch is a field the host serves
    /// (<c>pendingApprovalId</c>, an agent's <c>inbox</c>, the explicit <c>awaitingApproval</c> word) — the dot
    /// is never a status this page inferred from a quieter fact.
    /// </summary>
    private static string? PendingWhy(string? approvalId, bool inbox, bool awaitingStatus)
    {
        if (approvalId is { Length: > 0 })
            return $"waiting on approval {approvalId}";
        if (inbox)
            return "an interaction is waiting in the agent's inbox";
        if (awaitingStatus)
            return "the host's own status is awaitingApproval";
        return null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The first registered annotation that recognizes this runtime name, or no annotation.
    /// </summary>
    private string? SessionLabel(string? name) => Labels.Select(l => l.Label(name)).FirstOrDefault(l => l is not null);
}
